<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.13.3: Writing Equations that Represent a Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01971</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.13.3: Writing Equations that Represent a Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d7d5b3f5-60d7-449c-8a85-f90f9088b74b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <media alt=""><iframe src="../../media/desmos/a47b5bb4ba783be55a7067b919f165f14dcc36ce.html" width="500" height="400"/></media>
      <para id="para-00001">Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. Identify the function that matches each graph. Make sure your graph goes through all three points shown!</para>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00001">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00002">Identify the function of Graph A.</para>
            <para id="para-00003">
                      <media alt="Coordinate plane, graph of a quadratic function, point at negative 1 comma 1, minimum at 0 comma 0, point at 1 comma 1.&quot; height=&quot;197&quot;">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_01.svg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00004">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00005">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00006">\(y=x^2\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00002">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00007">Identify the function of Graph B.</para>
            <para id="para-00008">
                      <media alt="Coordinate plane, graph of a quadratic function, point at negative 3 comma 0, minimum at 0 comma negative 9, point at 3 comma 0.&quot; height=&quot;197&quot;">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_02.svg"/>
                
              </media>
          </para>
            <para id="para-00009">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00011">\(y=x^2-9\) or \(y=(x-3)(x+3)\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00003">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00012">Identify the function of Graph C.</para>
            <para id="para-00013">
                      <media alt="Coordinate plane, graph of a quadratic function, point at negative 2 comma 0, minimum at 0 point 5 comma negative 6 point 2 5, point at 3 comma 0.&quot; height=&quot;197&quot;">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_03.svg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00014">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00015">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00016">\(y=(x+2)(x-3)\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00004">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00017">Identify the function of Graph D.</para>
            <para id="para-00018">
                      <media alt="Coordinate plane, graph of a quadratic function, point at negative 6 comma 0, minimum at negative 3 comma negative 9, point at 0 comma 0.&quot; height=&quot;197&quot;">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_04.svg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00019">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00020">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00021">\(y=x(x+6)\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00005">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00022">Identify the function of Graph E.</para>
            <para id="para-00023">
                      <media alt="&quot;Coordinate plane, graph of a quadratic function, point at negative 2 comma 0, maximum at negative 0 comma 4, point at 2 comma 0.&quot; height=&quot;197&quot;">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_05.svg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00024">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00025">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00026">\(y=-x^2+4\) or \(y=(-x+2)(x+2)\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00006">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00027">Identify the function of Graph F.</para>
            <para id="para-00028">
                      <media alt="&quot;Coordinate plane, graph of a quadratic function, points at 0 comma 4, and 4 comma 4,&amp;nbsp;minimum at 2 comma 0.&quot; height=&quot;197&quot;">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_06.svg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00029">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00030">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00031">\(y=(x-2)(x-2)\) or \(y=x^2-4x+4\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00007">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00032">Identify the function of Graph G.</para>
            <para id="para-00033">
                      <media alt="&quot;Coordinate plane, graph of a quadratic function, point at negative 1 comma 0, maximum at 0 comma 3, point at 3 comma 0.&quot; height=&quot;197&quot;">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_07.svg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00034">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00035">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00036">\(y=(-x-1)(x-3)\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00008">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <para id="para-00037">Identify the function of Graph H.</para>
            <para id="para-00038">
                      <media alt="&quot;Coordinate plane, graph of a quadratic function, opens up, point at 0 comma 5, point at 1 comma 0, point at 5 comma 0.&quot; height=&quot;197&quot;">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_08.svg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00039">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00040">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00041">\(y=(x-1)(x-5)\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00009">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            <para id="para-00042">Identify the function of Graph I.</para>
            <para id="para-00043">
                      <media alt="&quot;Coordinate plane, graph of a quadratic function, point at negative 1 comma 2, minimum at 0 comma 0, point at 1 comma 2.&quot; height=&quot;197&quot;">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_09.svg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00044">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00045">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00046">\(y=2x^2\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      
        <exercise id="exer-00010">
          <problem id="prob-00010">
            <para id="para-00047">Identify the function of Graph J.</para>
            <para id="para-00048">
                      <media alt="Parabola. Opens down. Vertex at origin. Points on parabola include: -4 comma -4 and 4 comma -4.&quot; height=&quot;197&quot;">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_10.svg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00049">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00010">
            <para id="para-00050">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00051">\(y=-0.25x^2\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Video: Writing Equations that Represent a Quadratic Graph</title>
      <para id="para-00052">Watch the following video to learn more about writing equations that represent a quadratic graph.</para>
      <media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text">
        <iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/296f3aec8fb544a526585ba8f6a0ae3cdcf31337"/>
      </media>
    </section>

    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <para id="para-00053">Which equation describes the graph below?</para>
      <para id="para-00054">
          <media alt="GRAPH OF A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UPWARD WITH A \(y\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 12 AND \(x\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 4 AND 3.">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_07_01.png"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
    </note>

    <section id="sect-00003">
      <title>Writing Quadratic Equations from Graphs</title>
      <para id="para-00055">Write an equation for the graph below:</para>
      <para id="para-00056">
          <media alt="GRAPH OF A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UPWARD WITH A \(y\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 8 AND \(x\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 2 AND 4.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_08_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <para id="para-00057">First, locate the \(x\)-intercepts at \((-2,0)\) and \((4,0)\).
  Next, write the factor for each \(x\)-intercept.</para>
      <para id="para-00058">The factors that result in the given zeros are \((x + 2)\) and \((x - 4)\).
  The equation for this quadratic function is \(f(x)=(x + 2)(x - 4)\).</para>
      <para id="para-00059">Use graphing technology to check your answer.</para>
      <note class="try" id="note-00002">
  <title>Try It: Writing Quadratic Equations from Graphs</title>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00011">
          <problem id="prob-00011">
            <para id="para-00060">Write an equation for the graph below:</para>
            <para id="para-00061">
                      <media alt="GRAPH OF A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UPWARD WITH A \(y\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 12 AND \(x\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 6 AND 2.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_08_02.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00062">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00011">
            <para id="para-00063">Here is how to write an equation for the function graphed:</para>
            <para id="para-00064">First, identify the \(x\)-intercepts: \(x = -6\), \(x = 2.\)
    Next, write a factor for each zero:
    \((x + 6)\) and \((x - 2)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00065">The function in factored form is \(f(x)=(x + 6)(x - 2)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </note>
    </section>
  </content>
